ode7.irmos:
Once in Babylon the fire stood in awe of God's condescension;
for which sake the youths in the furnace, dancing with joyous steps as in a meadow, chanted://
O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou!

stichera.text:
Truly precious was the death of Thy saint in Thy sight, O Christ;
for, lo! a wellspring of blood poured forth from the foot of Thy favored one,
even after his death driving away every ailment
and expelling evil spirits against which he armed himself as a deadly opponent//
even while yet alive.
